      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-89522",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/5d/5d75d040ab38a9e14489c3df9d58883d2c85f8bd4c6f519cdc2224a2a3c0b500.png)\n\nA car windshield wiper, the arm and the blade combined, is $30$ inches long and swings back and forth through an angle of $120^{\u2218}$, as shown above. The shaded region in the figure is the portion of the windshield cleaned by the $20$-inch wiper blade. What is the area of the region cleaned by the blade?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
